From ef6e8e37d6b1d422521a80e67544152905117b21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raman Shinde <ramashin@blr-ubuntu-grtai02.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:34:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add gemm_coopmat cooperative-matrix example and Android
 cross-build support

Wires specialization constants, push constants, and VK_KHR_cooperative_matrix
feature negotiation into the core library, adds examples/gemm_coopmat.cc to
run and compare the gemm_kfirst / gemm_kfirst_tiled shaders, and adds a
VULKAN_APP_ANDROID CMake option so the same examples build and run on Android
(on-device shader path, validation layers off by default since the device
won't have the Khronos layer installed). Verified passing on-device: both
variants match the CPU reference, tiled layout ~1.24x faster.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
